Feature: Sales Data Processing in Unity Catalog Schema "purgo_playground"

  Background:
    Given the sample_sales_data.csv file is available 
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date  |
      | US         | P1001      | 50       | 2024-01-15  |
      | US         | P1002      | 30       | 2024-01-16  |
      | CA         | P1001      | 40       | 2024-01-15  |
      | CA         | P1003      | 25       | 2024-01-17  |
      | UK         | P1002      | 35       | 2024-01-18  |
      | UK         | P1004      | 20       | 2024-01-19  |
      | IN         | P1001      | 60       | 2024-01-20  |
      | IN         | P1003      | 45       | 2024-01-21  |
      | AU         | P1004      | 55       | 2024-01-22  |
      | AU         | P1002      | 38       | 2024-01-23  |
    And the data format is CSV
    And the data schema in the Unity Catalog is "purgo_playground"

  Scenario Outline: Successful Sales Data Import
    Given a CSV file with sales data is present
    When the data is imported to the Unity Catalog Schema "purgo_playground"
    Then the data should be present in the "sales_data" table
    And the data should match the format:
      | country_cd Varchar(2) | product_id Varchar(10) | qty_sold Integer | sales_date Date |
    Examples:
      | file_path                |
      | sample_sales_data.csv    |

  Scenario: Validation of Imported Data
    Given the sales data has been imported
    When querying for total product sales
    Then the sum of "qty_sold" should match expected values per product ID
    | product_id | expected_qty_sold |
    | P1001      | 150               |
    | P1002      | 103               |
    | P1003      | 70                |
    | P1004      | 75                |

  Scenario: Error Handling for Incorrect Data Format
    Given a CSV file with incorrect data format
    When trying to import this data
    Then an error should occur
    And the error message should be "Data Format Error: Invalid data format for sales_date"
    Examples:
      | file_path                     | incorrect_format                                       |
      | incorrect_sales_data.csv      | "country_cd, product_id, qty_sold, incorrect_date"     |

  Scenario: Error Handling for Missing Required Field
    Given a CSV file with missing fields
    When trying to import this data
    Then an error should occur
    And the error message should be "Data Import Error: Missing required field 'qty_sold'"
    Examples:
      | file_path                         | missing_field                                |
      | missing_qty_sold_data.csv         | "country_cd, product_id, sales_date"         |

